# Agentic StudyMate Cursor Rules

This file is the canonical architecture and AI-collaboration guide for Agentic StudyMate.
Future AI assistants must follow these rules before suggesting or changing code.

## Project Snapshot

Agentic StudyMate is a local-first multimodal RAG study assistant.

The application supports:

- Uploading PDF, DOCX, TXT, PNG, JPG/JPEG, and stored image documents.
- Hash-protected document ingestion with duplicate detection.
- Chat over documents through agentic RAG and multimodal RAG.
- Hybrid retrieval using semantic vectors, BM25 keyword search, reranking, and Neo4j graph context.
- Study tools such as quizzes, flashcards, and summaries.

## Mandatory Tech Stack

ALWAYS preserve this stack unless the user explicitly requests a migration:

- Backend: FastAPI, Python async endpoints, SQLAlchemy async sessions.
- Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4.
- Metadata database: SQLite through `aiosqlite`.
- Vector database: Qdrant at `localhost:6333`.
- GraphRAG database: Neo4j at `bolt://localhost:7687`.
- Embeddings: local CPU `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`.
- Reranker: local CPU `cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2`.
- Primary LLM provider: Groq.
- Text model: `meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct`.
- Vision model: `meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct`.

NEVER replace SQLite with PostgreSQL, Qdrant with another vector database, Neo4j with another graph store, or local CPU embeddings with hosted embeddings unless the user explicitly asks for that migration.

NEVER assume CUDA or GPU availability. All embedding and reranking code must remain CPU-compatible.

## Repository Map

Backend:

- `backend/app/main.py`: FastAPI app, CORS, static files, startup/shutdown lifespan, router mounting.
- `backend/app/config.py`: Pydantic settings and canonical model/database configuration.
- `backend/app/db/session.py`: async SQLAlchemy engine/session factory.
- `backend/app/db/init_db.py`: database creation, schema compatibility migrations, default user seeding, file hash backfill.
- `backend/app/models/db_models.py`: SQLAlchemy models.
- `backend/app/models/schemas.py`: API schemas.
- `backend/app/api/routes/upload.py`: document upload and text-document ingestion pipeline.
- `backend/app/api/routes/documents.py`: document listing/deletion plus image document processing and vision helpers.
- `backend/app/api/routes/chat.py`: SSE chat endpoint and image two-pass multimodal RAG.
- `backend/app/api/routes/study_tools.py`: quiz, flashcard, and summary generation.
- `backend/app/core/ingest/*`: extraction, chunking, embedding, graph triplet extraction.
- `backend/app/core/retrieval/*`: Qdrant vector store, BM25 store, hybrid retrieval.
- `backend/app/core/db/neo4j_client.py`: Neo4j GraphRAG client.
- `backend/app/core/agent/*`: query analysis, rewriting, planning, evaluation, generation, citation verification, LLM client.

Frontend:

- `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`: typed API client, upload calls, SSE chat parser.
- `frontend/src/pages/Upload.tsx`: drag-and-drop uploads and duplicate upload handling.
- `frontend/src/pages/Chat.tsx`: streaming chat UI and image chat flow.
- `frontend/src/pages/Library.tsx`: document library and delete flow.
- `frontend/src/pages/StudyTools.tsx`: generated study tools UI.
- `frontend/src/components/*`: shared layout, document, chat, quiz, and flashcard components.

## Unified LLM Strategy

ALWAYS use Groq as the primary and required LLM provider for new work.

ALWAYS use `meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct` for both:

- `TEXT_MODEL`
- `VISION_MODEL`

ALWAYS route text calls through the project LLM client instead of creating ad hoc provider clients.

ALWAYS route vision/multimodal calls through `get_llm_client().call_multimodal(...)`.

ALWAYS format Groq multimodal payloads with OpenAI-compatible content parts:

```python
messages = [
    {"role": "system", "content": system_prompt},
    {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
            {"type": "text", "text": prompt},
            {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": image_url}},
        ],
    },
]
```

ALWAYS pass images as HTTP(S) URLs, local/static URLs loaded by the backend, or `data:image/...;base64,...` URLs.

ALWAYS resize images before vision calls using the existing helper path in `documents.py`; preserve the JPEG normalization for OpenAI-compatible multimodal payloads.

NEVER suggest or introduce legacy text or vision models such as Gemini, OpenAI GPT, Anthropic Claude, or older Llama variants for new functionality.

NEVER add new provider fallbacks for new features. Legacy provider code may still exist in the repository, but it is not the architectural target.

NEVER use separate text and vision model families. The project decision is one unified Groq Scout model for both text and vision.

## Deduplication Shield

Uploads must be protected by SHA-256 hashing.

ALWAYS hash uploaded file bytes before saving a text document.

ALWAYS check `Document.file_hash` in SQLite before creating a new document record.

ALWAYS keep `Document.file_hash` unique in the database.

ALWAYS return HTTP `409 Conflict` when a duplicate hash already exists.

ALWAYS include duplicate metadata in the 409 response when available:

```json
{
  "message": "File already exists in the library",
  "document_id": "<existing document id>",
  "file_name": "<existing file name>",
  "status": "<existing status>"
}
```

ALWAYS handle race conditions with the database unique constraint, not only with a pre-insert SELECT.

ALWAYS delete the newly written duplicate file from disk if an `IntegrityError` proves the hash already exists.

ALWAYS keep the frontend duplicate behavior graceful:

- Detect `response.status === 409`.
- Do not crash the upload flow.
- Show the user-facing toast message exactly: `File already exists in the library!`
- Still record the duplicate as an upload result/error if the UI has an upload results list.

NEVER bypass hashing for PDF, DOCX, or TXT uploads.

NEVER silently re-ingest duplicate files.

NEVER treat duplicate upload as a generic 500-class error.

## Two-Pass Agentic Multimodal RAG

The chat endpoint uses a two-pass flow whenever an image is attached.

ALWAYS use Pass 1 for image chat:

1. Send the image plus the user prompt to the vision model.
2. Extract 3 to 5 technical keywords, entities, or concepts.
3. Output only a concise comma-separated retrieval query.

ALWAYS use Pass 2 for image chat:

1. Use the extracted keywords to retrieve context from Qdrant/BM25 and Neo4j.
2. Combine the original image, the original user prompt, and retrieved context.
3. Ask the same Groq Scout vision model to produce the final answer.
4. Return citations derived from retrieved chunks and graph-backed chunks.

ALWAYS include both retrieval sources for image RAG:

- Vector/BM25 passages from Qdrant and the BM25 index.
- Neo4j GraphRAG relationships linked back to SQLite chunk IDs.

ALWAYS preserve the current SSE event contract:

- `session`
- `status`
- `chunk`
- `citations`
- `done`
- `error`

ALWAYS bypass Pass 1 for text-only chat requests. Text-only requests should use the normal agentic text RAG pipeline.

NEVER answer an image chat directly from the image when the user is asking against the study library. The required flow is image keywords -> retrieval -> image + prompt + context final answer.

NEVER use OCR-only image extraction as the final answer path for chat.

NEVER drop the original user prompt in Pass 2. The final synthesis must include image, prompt, and context.

## Text RAG Pipeline

For text-only chat, preserve the agentic pipeline:

1. Analyze the question.
2. Rewrite for retrieval.
3. Plan sub-questions when needed.
4. Retrieve with hybrid search.
5. Rerank with the local cross-encoder.
6. Evaluate context sufficiency and retry if appropriate.
7. Generate an answer with citations.
8. Verify citations.

ALWAYS cite answers using retrieved source metadata.

ALWAYS keep fallback behavior graceful when external services are unavailable.

NEVER replace the agentic pipeline with single-step basic RAG unless explicitly requested.

## Retrieval Rules

ALWAYS use `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` embeddings with 384-dimensional vectors.

ALWAYS keep Qdrant collection vectors configured for cosine distance.

ALWAYS use Qdrant on port `6333`.

ALWAYS preserve payload metadata for vector points:

- `document_id`
- `chunk_id`
- `chunk_index`
- `content`
- `page_number`
- `section_title`
- `image_url` when applicable

ALWAYS keep BM25 as a complementary keyword index.

ALWAYS use Reciprocal Rank Fusion for merging vector and BM25 results in hybrid retrieval.

ALWAYS rerank final candidates with the CPU cross-encoder for text RAG.

NEVER store vectors without enough metadata to reconstruct citations.

NEVER make Qdrant failure fatal to ingestion if BM25 can still work.

## GraphRAG Rules

ALWAYS use Neo4j on `bolt://localhost:7687` for GraphRAG when configured.

ALWAYS store extracted triplets as entity relationships tagged with the source SQLite `chunk_id`.

ALWAYS sanitize Neo4j relationship types before interpolating them into Cypher.

ALWAYS retrieve graph relationships by matching entity/relation text and map results back to source chunks for citations.

NEVER interpolate unsanitized relationship names into Cypher.

NEVER return graph context without a path back to source chunk citations when citations are needed.

## Ingestion Rules

ALWAYS follow this text-document ingestion order:

1. Validate file type.
2. Read bytes.
3. Hash bytes.
4. Reject duplicates with 409.
5. Save file.
6. Create `Document(status="processing")`.
7. Extract text.
8. Chunk text.
9. Store chunks in SQLite.
10. Extract/store Neo4j triplets.
11. Generate local CPU embeddings.
12. Upsert vectors into Qdrant.
13. Add chunks to BM25.
14. Mark document `ready` or `failed`.

ALWAYS mark documents as `failed` if extraction produces no chunks or the pipeline raises.

ALWAYS keep database commits and rollbacks explicit around upload and ingestion transitions.

NEVER add new file types without updating validation, extraction, frontend accepted types, and schemas together.

## Frontend Rules

ALWAYS use the existing typed API client in `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`.

ALWAYS preserve SSE parsing for streaming chat.

ALWAYS support image chat by sending multipart `FormData` with:

- `question`
- optional `document_ids` JSON string
- optional `session_id`
- `image`

ALWAYS keep duplicate upload handling centralized around 409 detection.

ALWAYS show duplicate uploads as the toast text `File already exists in the library!`.

NEVER let duplicate uploads crash the page or break subsequent uploads in the same batch.

NEVER change API paths casually; the frontend and backend are coupled around `/api/upload`, `/api/documents`, `/api/documents/image`, `/api/chat`, and `/api/study-tools/*`.

## Configuration Rules

Required local service defaults:

```env
DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./studymate.db
QDRANT_HOST=localhost
QDRANT_PORT=6333
NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
TEXT_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct
VISION_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct
EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=384
RERANKER_MODEL=cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2
```

ALWAYS load settings from `backend/app/config.py`.

ALWAYS keep model names configurable through settings but defaulted to the required Groq Scout model.

NEVER hardcode API keys.

NEVER commit `.env`, local databases, uploaded files, or generated Qdrant storage.

## API Contracts

Core endpoints:

- `GET /api/health`
- `POST /api/upload`
- `GET /api/documents`
- `GET /api/documents/{document_id}`
- `DELETE /api/documents/{document_id}`
- `POST /api/documents/image`
- `POST /api/chat`
- `GET /api/chat/sessions`
- `GET /api/chat/sessions/{session_id}`
- `DELETE /api/chat/sessions/{session_id}`
- `POST /api/study-tools/quiz`
- `POST /api/study-tools/flashcards`
- `POST /api/study-tools/summary`

ALWAYS preserve response shapes used by the frontend schemas in `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`.

NEVER change an endpoint contract without updating backend schemas, frontend types, and all callers together.

## Testing And Verification

For backend changes:

- Run targeted Python checks or tests where available.
- At minimum, run import/compile checks for touched backend modules.
- Verify duplicate upload behavior when touching ingestion/upload code.
- Verify image chat SSE events when touching multimodal chat.

For frontend changes:

- Run `npm run build` when TypeScript or React code changes.
- Verify duplicate upload 409 handling when touching upload UI/API code.
- Verify streaming chat if touching `streamChat` or chat UI state.

For architecture-rule changes:

- Re-read `backend/app/config.py`, `backend/app/api/routes/upload.py`, `backend/app/api/routes/chat.py`, `backend/app/api/routes/documents.py`, and `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`.

NEVER claim a behavior is verified unless you actually ran the relevant check.

## Future AI Assistant Rules

ALWAYS read this file before making architectural suggestions.

ALWAYS inspect current code before changing behavior.

ALWAYS preserve the explicit decisions in this file over generic best practices.

ALWAYS mention any existing code that conflicts with these instructions before expanding it.

NEVER suggest legacy provider migrations.

NEVER simplify away deduplication, GraphRAG, hybrid retrieval, citation metadata, or the two-pass image RAG design.

NEVER introduce unrelated refactors while fixing a focused issue.

NEVER overwrite user work or generated local data unless explicitly asked.
